# Server-only. Create a key at https://console.typesafe.ai/keys
# and paste it here. Next.js reads this file on the server.
# Do not rename it to NEXT_PUBLIC_JEV_API_KEY. That would ship the key to the browser.
#
# When this is set, live transcripts go to Jev
# (POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone, model jev-latest)
# through @typesafe-ai/sdk. The official client otherwise reads TYPESAFE_API_KEY;
# this app passes JEV_API_KEY explicitly and ignores that default.
#
# When this is empty, or a call fails, the deterministic parser is used.
# Demo playback always uses the parser so the scripted order stays exact.
JEV_API_KEY=

# Server-only. AssemblyAI streaming speech-to-text (model universal-3-6-pro).
# https://www.assemblyai.com/dashboard — never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# The browser only receives a short-lived streaming token from /api/assemblyai-token.
# When this is empty, or the token or socket fails, speech falls back to Chrome.
ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=
